                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bc810601-9e48-365a-8337-850658bcc9d1",
                        "entry_id": "727d6476-aed7-3533-9050-357dba2a0149",
                        "glosses": [
                            "lightly; gently or without great force."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "542133b6-9278-481b-b3ef-2794f1e0ef8d",
                                "sense_id": "bc810601-9e48-365a-8337-850658bcc9d1",
                                "text": "I will mak a lang ladder, Wi' fifty steps and three, three, I will mak a lang ladder, And lichtly come doun to thee, thee, And lichtly come doun to thee."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf3e71bc-a970-4975-99bd-5f234e3f30b9",
                                "sense_id": "bc810601-9e48-365a-8337-850658bcc9d1",
                                "text": "Saft in his arms he caught her up, Winsome Annie Ramsay. An' swang her lichtly to the croup, Winsome Annie Ramsay."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad8e98f3-e030-4a29-a5bd-7a9a3220f592",
                                "sense_id": "bc810601-9e48-365a-8337-850658bcc9d1",
                                "text": "Than, tae her gret surprise, he touched her hair, sae lichtly that she cud haurdly feel it, an rinnin a finger doonwart, he fund her yae lang braid an pickit it up."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "420374ff-e45b-3be9-8507-6e5d6cdee214",
                        "entry_id": "727d6476-aed7-3533-9050-357dba2a0149",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a manner that is not serious."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e11812cb-19d2-461b-9731-8f590dbb643e",
                                "sense_id": "420374ff-e45b-3be9-8507-6e5d6cdee214",
                                "text": "Weel, time gaed by: and the idler sort commenced to think mair lichtly o' that black business."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1c0a4cb-981b-4eb6-89e9-a46c0ea2f8fa",
                                "sense_id": "420374ff-e45b-3be9-8507-6e5d6cdee214",
                                "text": "But a wuman wha wad sae misguide the son o' her ain body, an' for naething but that as she had broucht him furth sic he was, — it \"s no to be lichtly believed nor lichtly endured."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91d71dc3-0a59-4b5e-b2c5-c0359b013c3a",
                                "sense_id": "420374ff-e45b-3be9-8507-6e5d6cdee214",
                                "text": "“Dinna speak sae lichtly, Thamas,\" remonstrated his wife. “"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
